; bars remain limited to padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, wrapping, scroll/ruler/completion mapping and suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture, journal, new-file, picker, menu, help, find and supersampling repairs. Preserve ruler presentation, faithful Unicode/style diagnostics and strict native styled-widget/compositor equality.\n- Preserve mount-hook ordering: workspace completion/restoration, one database switch/restoration, one command-focus request, then readiness after actual queued focus application. Production callbacks execute unchanged and exactly once; later focus loss rejects readiness without repair. Retain border diagnostics without selecting an unproven border repair.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub acceptance\n\nAll execution occurs through the authorized GitHub mechanisms. Private workers perform source-only work.\n\n1. Obtain fresh separate independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding.\n2. Verify fixture envelope decoding against both original captured hashes. Reject malformed base64, length/hash mismatches and altered decoded bytes. Preserve all causal raster assertions.\n3. Run real resvg/Pillow regressions on the unmodified captured exports and normalized outputs using the same independently mapped caret regions and visibility predicate. Require the original failure and repaired visibility to be demonstrated, including command-focus persistence and keyboard primary/secondary carets. Retain no-underline, wrong-cell, wrong-color, clipping and period-versus-underline controls.\n4. Exercise whitespace, expanded tabs, wide/combining glyphs, inherited/nested spans, transforms, clipping, color/opacity preservation, duplicate-decoration prevention, unsupported inputs and idempotence. Retain real widget/compositor preservation assertions.\n5. Run new-file fixture/mounted alignment, deterministic delayed-mount, ruler/styled-row, diagnostic non-mutation, comparison-budget and capture-lifecycle suites across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1. Run restored dev regressions and focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret/completion, journal, menu and checkbox coverage.\n6. Require exact-final-head lint/format/type/quality, canonical coverage, artifacts, runtime/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Preserve **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement** floors, subsystem floors and debt baselines. Use actual new coverage JSON for any further task-related regression correction.\n7. Through the existing signed temporary-candidate/legacy capture route, retain fresh original and normalized stage PNG/SVG evidence, actual intermediate bytes, versions, font observations, renderer arguments and complete source/checkpoint/base/task/plan/candidate/producer/run/job/attempt/artifact bindings. Font availability or `fc-match` never proves renderer selection.\n8. Independently inspect every retained full stage PNG and all **46 full 1280×800 scene PNGs at 208×47 cells**. Require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass before correction publication. Keep existing rejections effective until fresh acceptance; inconclusive reproduction requires renewed planning, not adjusted assertions.\n9. Complete independent whole-feature/source and companion assessment of every diff continuation. Historical captures, successful diagnostics and partial reviews certify no new content.\n\n## Delivery and completion\n\nRecheck head, base, request revision, provenance, authority and actual holds at every action boundary; revalidate if content or dev advances. Preserve inherited native/source-validation safeguards without deploying them or inventing an upstream PR prerequisite for PR #9.\n\nRetain genuine credential/security, owner-input/veto/cancel, operational and applicable exact-head protected gates. Do not alter frozen rollout bytes, repeat completed deployments or take over handed-off branches.\n\nThe coordinator must verify recommendation-policy companion completion, independent resolution records, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve authenticated Q/A, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, and one 30-minute open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n\nPreserve dependency direction: #10 requires #9’s actual dev merge/ancestry; #37 retains its separate #39 dependency. Continue monitoring and aligned repairs until #9 and every qualifying companion/correction/repair PR successfully merge into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This correction alone does not complete that parent objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a55bf7b312a52313013a3dc4022f66541ebf53db1441215f687f1caddb048783","text":"# Preserve PR #9 and obtain decisive compatibility and raster evidence\n\n## Summary\n\nBind this plan to pinned dev `4a17e91b20b2683aca365f486e6217a141ef8c5b`, published head `dba63c219c7b9923b433d546e92d674406406df5`, and the actual saved checkpoint.\n\nRun `39313698235` confirms Python 3.9 renderer installation failure, four raster regression failures on Python 3.10–3.14, and lint/format failures. Saved diagnostic additions have not yet been validated.\n\nImplement the recorded **Compatibility probe** and **Causal diagnostics** decisions. No additional owner choice is required for this diagnostic checkpoint. Dependency adoption, visibility-predicate changes, and further rendering repairs require evidence and a separately reviewed concrete plan.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Preserve the complete feature patch, recovered source/documentation, fixture envelopes, authenticated chronological history and all useful saved diagnostics. Reconcile incoming dev without removing inherited capture, authority, lifecycle or workflow safeguards. Fully read each file before editing.\n- Finish behavior-preserving quality corrections identified in the complete log:\n  - E501 in the SVG-evidence helper; PLW2901 in the underline normalizer; PLC0414 in normalized-comparison tests.\n  - I001 in styled-row, underline-geometry and rasterization tests; SIM117 in rasterization tests.\n  - Formatting in the eight reported diagnostic, scene, fixture and test modules.\n  Preserve fixture bytes, callback order, parameters, assertions, negative controls and diagnostic output. Use Ruff 0.15.22 and repository configuration through GitHub; add no suppressions or baseline changes.\n- Preserve and finish `tests/agent_tools/_support/renderer_probe.py`. Within each Python 3.9 latest/minimum GitHub job, create a disposable environment and investigate the saved `resvg-py==0.3.2` probe candidate. Retain actual downloaded wheel identity and metadata, installation report, API-rendered PNG, identical raster cases, `pip check`, frozen dependencies, command arguments, exit status and bounded stdout/stderr.\n- Keep `resvg-py>=0.5,<0.6` ordinary requirements unchanged during diagnosis. The probe must neither replace the ordinary environment nor turn a failed required job green. An older renderer’s compatibility and behavioral equivalence remain unproven.\n- Finish the saved raster-observation collector and its integration with `tests/agent_tools/underline_rasterization.py`. Before strict assertions, collect both captured scenes and synthetic space, expanded-tab, wide-glyph and combining-mark cases. Retain original, plain, normalized and applicable wrong-color/clipped controls, plus wrong-cell observations.\n- Retain exact input/supersampling SVGs and actual direct, 2× intermediate and once-reduced PNG bytes. Record mapped regions, sampled RGB values and differences, qualifying runs, unchanged thresholds, predicate results, conversion records, versions, renderer arguments and observable font-file identities.\n- Preserve `_target_regions`, `_visible_underline`, normalization geometry, captured fixture hashes and every causal assertion during this step. Identify separate diagnostic reproductions truthfully; do not label them as bytes from the strict test invocation or historical capture.\n- Use the existing test-workflow artifact uploads and canonical coverage transport. Preserve ordinary aggregate checks and inherited diagnostic-mode guards. Diagnostic failure must retain evidence and must not prevent subsequent strict checks where installation succeeded.\n- Correct stale diagnostic bindings: retain historical plan/head identities as historical fields and bind new reports to the actual reviewed plan, task, checkpoint, source files, base, candidate, profile, run/job/attempt and artifact receipts. Do not substitute hardcoded historical hashes for current provenance.\n- Preserve separate 4 MiB SVG/decoded-PNG comparison budgets, existing diagnostic bounds and 8 MiB per-file/64 MiB artifact limits. Missing, oversized or failed observations remain explicitly incomplete.\n- Update focused diagnostic documentation and the existing managed changelog fragment. Preserve release history and package/README versions.\n\n## Complete behavior and compatibility retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections without spawning cursors. Preserve independent preferred columns, reversal, clamping, boundaries, same-row multicursors, selection merging and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles.\n- Preserve document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; all-empty multicursor clearing without deletion; and single unselected whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation, empty-paste behavior, atomic undo/redo, bounded history/pruning and reset cleanup.\n- Preserve thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, wrapping, selections, scrolling, ruler/completion mapping and suffixes.\n- Retain all selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, supersampling, faithful Unicode/style diagnostics, raw-strip fidelity and strict native-styled-widget/compositor equality.\n- Preserve mount-hook ordering, production callbacks exactly once, strict readiness/focus/non-mutation assertions and delayed-mount regressions. Keep inherited ruler presentation and the reported first-line/ruler finding unresolved pending fresh independent reassessment.\n- Public APIs, runtime dependencies, `>=3.8,<3.15` metadata and Python 3.8 static compatibility remain unchanged. Preserve Python 3.9–3.14 runtime profiles, `py39-min`, both Python 3.10 SDK profiles and minimum pins. Diagnostic report fields remain additive.\n\n## Focused coverage and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, imports, installations, tests, probes and rendering run through authorized GitHub mechanisms; private workers perform source-only work.\n\n1. Obtain fresh independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding.\n2. Run diagnostic support regressions first: dependency-free probe bootstrap, wheel metadata identity, original command streams/status, timeout/capacity reporting, continued collection after failures, exact fixture decoding, stage dimensions/hashes, one reduction and observation non-mutation.\n3. Run disposable Python 3.9 probes in both profiles. On canonical Python 3.11 and supported latest environments, retain every causal case before executing unchanged strict raster assertions. Expected diagnostic failures remain failures.\n4. Independently inspect all retained full images, mapped cells and pixel/color runs. Explain original false-positive visibility, wide-glyph rejection and combining-mark wrong-color acceptance from actual evidence before proposing corrections. Record replay differences and unknown renderer-selected fonts honestly.\n5. Reassess `tab-database-change` using fresh full PNG, separate ruler/editor regions, first gutter/text rows, native styled/compositor rows and lifecycle evidence. Retain overlap, shifted-mapping, missing-label/gutter and trailing-cell controls. Do not change presentation or expected values to force acceptance.\n6. Run adjacent multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, caret/completion, mounted new-file alignment, mount-ordering, ruler, journal, menu and capture regressions.\n7. After independently planned repairs, require exact-final-head lint/format/type/quality, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, runtime/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Preserve at least **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement coverage**, all subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n8. Obtain newly bound caret comparisons: both scenes, both font declarations and all three stages—twelve complete original stage PNGs—plus separately labeled normalized comparisons. Preserve exact originals and actual intermediate bytes.\n9. Before correction publication, require complete independent feature/source/companion assessment, all **46 geometry checks** and individual full **1280×800 PNG verdicts at 208×47 cells**. Successful collection is not visual approval; historical receipts certify no new edits.\n\n## Delivery and completion\n\nUse the established temporary-candidate capture and ordinary CI routes. The trusted coordinator rechecks actual routing, producer/consumer compatibility, source/head/base/task, authorization and current holds at each action boundary. Preserve inherited native-validation sources without inferring activation or creating a new PR #9 prerequisite.\n\nKeep existing rejections effective until fresh independent acceptance. Inconclusive diagnostics require renewed planning. Implement no speculative renderer downgrade, font switch, caret primitive or border/ruler repair.\n\nPreserve genuine security, credentials, provenance, owner-input/veto/cancel, operational and protected exact-head gates; frozen rollout bytes; and completed/cancelled operations.\n\nRetain recommendation-policy companion work, independent resolution records and safe recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated complete Q/A, notification limits and one 30-minute open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n\nMaintain dependency direction: #10 requires #9’s actual dev merge/ancestry; #37 retains its separate #39 dependency. Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until #9 and every qualifying companion/correction/repair PR merge successfully into `dev` with required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that parent objective.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","questions":[{"answer_index":16,"id":"fbd480038ee660edb95dd3690683161a39480ffc41dfac01f8e147887794ef84","text":"Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export."},{"answer_index":18,"id":"9a11147e3ffd85ce140c8f1244a1b15377efd00916e606a8b431a2d03a92488d","text":"The fresh receipt binds capture `38731476440` to candidate `3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5` and the saved checkpoint. Widget rows, compositor rows and parsed SVG all retain the complete heading, including the `c`. This does not establish a production picker defect.\n\n1. **Coordinator tooling question:** Can `read_evidence_image` be exposed in this planner session for the supplied hash-bound PNG? It is absent from the available tools, and `read_image` returns “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” PNG inspection is still needed before specifying a presentation or export correction.\n\nNo owner decision or replacement upload is needed. Raw SVG bytes are not supplied. The publication transport repair also remains coordinator-owned; complete task history must be preserved."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"16d4d781180edfb004dda9a37d5c640ea072ea2cc5775a4681e92c27f584ab07","text":"Can the coordinator provide the reviewed plan’s GitHub reproduction with actual raw and framed SVG bytes, renderer versions, and available/selected font diagnostics, bound to the candidate, checkpoint and PNG hashes? PNG inspection now works and confirms the obscured `c`; terminal rows and parsed SVG preserve it. The supplied artifacts still cannot distinguish framing from rasterization, so a correction would be speculative."},{"answer_index":20,"id":"9d7dfd33ccfb0fff403dc64cf5154bb0084c6d340b3db71751df45304dbb3650","text":"Coordinator: please expose the exact pre-invocation checkpoint source for tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py. I mistakenly treated a capped 300-line read as complete and omitted its remaining lines when writing. Restore that file’s original suffix before retaining my focused additions. Please also verify the restored README against the saved checkpoint. No owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":21,"id":"962ad2658075e133178b0c27a43c436c00ea5a63640a4a6e0dafbca91a41dc09","text":"Coordinator: please run the approved isolated GitHub candidate capture from the preserved checkpoint, including the restored diagnostic tests and existing SVG-evidence helper/tests. Expose hash-bound database-picker raw/framed SVG content, font/renderer diagnostics and PNG through source_files. The reviewed plan requires this evidence before selecting a heading correction; no owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":22,"id":"d82141d33b770fcc68e14949f0292959e0f2597aa4301b71d32ab7338f57b0e7","text":"1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together."},{"answer_index":23,"id":"e896f2e46da935a3d8d2023d77a872fd7f6624fbdae4625988d391767b3be2a6","text":"I read the complete current-head check records and all failed-job log parts. Existing feature requirements remain settled; no new owner preference is needed. Three coordinator evidence questions remain before a concrete repair plan:\n\n1. **Picker correction:** Can the coordinator expose capture `38927473247`’s hash-bound receipt, database-picker geometry, complete raw/framed SVGs, and all four comparison PNGs? The visual evidence tools currently return “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” The reviewer’s framing finding needs direct inspection before selecting the export correction.\n\n2. **Coverage:** Can the coordinator expose canonical `coverage.json` from run `38927048857`, bound to head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2`? Branch coverage is **98.02% against 98.03%**. Exact missing arcs are needed to specify meaningful task-related regressions without changing baselines.\n\n3. **Type-menu failure:** Can the coordinator provide a bounded GitHub reproduction capturing focus, `type_input`, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry, and queued layout state immediately before the failing initial `assert menu.display` on Python 3.13/3.14? This will distinguish fixture timing from a production positioning defect before choosing a repair.\n\nThese are coordinator artifact requests, not requests for owner uploads or approval. No files were changed and no programs were executed."},{"answer_index":24,"id":"b239df38a3cbbd33de3627b25a36e9063e036dac68b6e9c97c83d69c701c88f3","text":"1. The rejected PNG and widget/compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: rendering replaces the existing separator space with a bar. Should the correction preserve every in-document whitespace cell using the thin underline fallback, reserving vertical bars for end-of-line and empty-line padding?\nPreserve whitespace (Recommended): Keep spaces and expanded tabs intact for primary and secondary carets; retain colors, cell widths and completion behavior, and add focused rendering and completion regressions."},{"answer_index":25,"id":"ba800d0ea428ec7a001c0765a90362402cdfe85aa29ac8ae5d7e49a96975ad4b","text":"1. Should the plan restore the newly pinned dev’s capture/export safeguards before completing the outstanding independent review? The current diff deletes `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`, its regression module and a parent-objective record, reverts `agent-visual.yml`, and removes failed-capture documentation.\nPreserve dev safeguards (Recommended): Restore those files and workflow exactly from pinned dev, retain its documentation plus the feature-specific activation section, preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch, then obtain fresh review and GitHub validation.\nReview before reconciliation: Complete read-only assessment of the published predecessor first; keep current-base reconciliation and final candidate validation blocked until separately planned."},{"answer_index":26,"id":"7955d1db22074defa82b9d57196aac7ba36a0679d4226fe9ad241de670ff3d1e","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the inherited column ruler and route the reported stray “1” for independent reassessment, using the inspected PNG, separate ruler/editor geometry, identical pinned-dev ruler source, and existing empty-document assertion? This resolves the correction approach only; the rejecting visual gate remains in force until independently reviewed.\nPreserve ruler (Recommended): Preserve production presentation; add a focused tab-switch ruler/gutter regression and explicit scene evidence, then repeat independent full-feature and visual review.\nChange ruler presentation: Authorize a narrow presentation change to distinguish column labels from gutter numbers; its exact appearance needs a further decision before implementation."},{"answer_index":27,"id":"46377a331dc01c2e34cff52b83d9ddd5e5dd1b98a41de0000d6832f0d20a0a45","text":"1. Should the renewed plan first collect bounded, GitHub-only evidence for the indistinct secondary carets before choosing a production or export repair? The inspected PNG confirms the visibility finding, but its geometry does not identify the failing layer.\nDiagnose first (Recommended): Preserve the complete feature and selected ruler work; add exact cursor/focus/scroll state, caret-cell widget/compositor styles and lossless SVG evidence with focused regressions, then independently plan the demonstrated repair after GitHub capture.\nChange caret presentation: Plan a production presentation change now; its precise appearance requires another choice and must preserve SQL, whitespace, colors, widths and mapping."},{"answer_index":28,"id":"1533c21a5bce25f66a9d4d6d9395969fe2d15e25112b4e9000ea13507588cdd7","text":"1. May the renewed plan include narrow repairs for the newly verified journal-error status and new-file dialog alignment, after identifying their failing layers? These extend the earlier enumerated UI repair scope.\nNarrow gate repairs (Recommended): Show read failures without claiming empty results, restore intended dialog centering, add focused regressions, and retain the complete feature and all review gates.\n\n2. Should the correction fix the confirmed diagnostic/test defects and collect missing command-caret and ruler lifecycle evidence before selecting further presentation or focus changes?\nFaithful diagnostics (Recommended): Fix variable shadowing and lint, preserve combining marks and cell styles during cropping, retain strict assertions, and diagnose ruler focus/width and command-caret layers on GitHub without forcing scene state."},{"answer_index":29,"id":"310ef79ccea7f258fef9f5fee47aebad16404f96b3ab0e5fc0e03fac1fad6e90","text":"1. Which correction sequence should the renewed plan specify for the observed ruler focus and row-width failures? Existing assertions and production ruler presentation must remain intact.\nTrace lifecycle (Recommended): Fix the confirmed lint/format findings, preserve current-dev safeguards, and add bounded GitHub-only callback-order and strip-padding observations before selecting the focus or width correction.\nCorrect scene lifecycle: Plan command focus after tab restoration and full-width widget-row collection now; retain strict equality and negative controls, then require GitHub reproduction and independent review."},{"answer_index":30,"id":"fd123ca6bb2e97c0179d0650913397f70c39425e6f71229ff3f98ad248a446a7","text":"1. Should the renewed plan correct the demonstrated harness-layer mismatch: apply the scene’s intended command focus after deferred tab restoration, and compare Textual’s styled widget rows with compositor rows while retaining the original unpadded strips as separate evidence? Production tab behavior and ruler presentation would stay unchanged; strict equality, negative controls, and all feature/review gates remain required.\nCorrect harness layers (Recommended): Use ordered scene initialization and native styled-row collection, preserve raw observations, fix confirmed lint/format findings, and validate on GitHub.\nExtend diagnostics first: Preserve the failing harness and collect native styled-row and focus-application traces on GitHub before separately planning its correction."},{"answer_index":31,"id":"4eabbb1c0750e4fc0765750745d410dec1b52cf5617089e9dfd9c6176b220bff","text":"1. Should the renewed correction replace the tab/database scene’s fixed 0.3-second switch timer with the existing workspace mount-completion hook, ordering database switching after workspace initialization and its deferred restoration, then applying command focus once? The Python 3.12 trace shows workspace completion arriving after scene initialization; preserve every strict ordering assertion, production tab behavior, and the complete feature.\nOrder mount completion (Recommended): Use the existing pending_mount_action hook and ordered scene continuations; add a deterministic delayed-mount regression, correct lint/format findings, and require independent review plus GitHub CI and all 46 visual scenes."},{"answer_index":32,"id":"659c61c7bd86b5bbc53d59c646f62f30d7371c88f1dafedfd973d6d8ac09aa59","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the complete checkpoint and selected mount-ordering correction, fix the confirmed import/format findings, and obtain six GitHub-only caret raster comparisons before selecting an export repair? The latest coordinator report supplies a recommendation, not an approved implementation choice.\nSix comparisons (Recommended): For keyboard-multicursor and editor-command-caret, retain direct, actual 2× intermediate, and reduced PNGs under original declarations and a diagnostic-only verified DejaVu Sans Mono declaration; preserve production rendering, exact SVG/settings/font hashes, bounded lossless evidence, all assertions and review gates."},{"answer_index":33,"id":"706b7cb93eb62f050815bd403f89b787ee00056be012dbafa618eeda9492f614","text":"The feature choices are settled. Current-head run `39133140732` confirms import ordering, formatting, and a mount-ordering failure (`20 < 11`). The saved checkpoint already contains mount-hook work; those earlier failures cannot validate it.\n\nTwo coordinator questions remain before a complete plan can pass independent review. No owner preference or upload is needed.\n\n1. **Capture prerequisites:** Can the coordinator provide current, source-pinned evidence identifying the authorized isolated GitHub capture route, producer/consumer revisions, artifact compatibility, activation state, and applicable operational/protected holds? It must establish whether the selected twelve retained caret-stage PNGs and border diagnostics can be collected without modifying frozen deployments or overriding holds.\n\n2. **Prerequisite representation:** Can the coordinator resolve those external conditions and supply their evidence, or provide a separately reviewed supported mechanism for retaining them in the plan-review contract? The previous independent review rejected the plan because these conditions cannot be represented as `pr_dev_merge`. They must not be omitted or converted into fictitious PR dependencies.\n\nPR #10’s dependency on #9, and #37’s dependency on #39, remain downstream obligations—not prerequisites for #9.\n\nI’m stopping with these evidence questions rather than issuing another plan with unresolved consequential prerequisites. No files were edited or programs executed."},{"answer_index":34,"id":"1f4786be9b181443cf96946f2a96c395e841d6f855d3911ccf6a8fbdc95a336f","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve pinned dev 388b2eb’s capture-isolation/source-validation files, tests, evidence records and workflow safeguards, removing the saved patch’s stale reversions while retaining all SQL Explorer changes? This reconciles source only; actual deployed capture routing and protected approvals remain coordinator checks.\nPreserve current dev (Recommended): Restore inherited safeguards from immutable dev, retain feature-specific diagnostic additions, and require fresh independent review and GitHub validation.\nAssess reversions separately: Keep reconciliation blocked while the coordinator supplies a separately reviewed justification for each inherited safeguard removal.\n\n2. Should validation follow pinned dev’s Python 3.9–3.14 runtime matrix and Python 3.9 minimum environment, retaining public Python 3.8 metadata/static syntax compatibility? Earlier plans used Python 3.8 runtime environments, which the saved patch currently reinstates.\nPreserve dev matrix (Recommended): Remove stale Python 3.8 runtime-profile reversions, retain required Pillow test dependencies and coverage artifacts, and preserve public Python 3.8 compatibility.\nRetain Python 3.8 runs: Explicitly retain Python 3.8 runtime coverage in addition to dev’s Python 3.9 minimum environment, requiring reviewed compatibility configuration."},{"answer_index":35,"id":"643a4b634d7bcf859d32cb1ec804db30a977fb67e2b35d7e66f4af3c2951d3f0","text":"1. Should the correction complete the fake new-file screen in tests/agent_tools/visual_evidence.py with centered viewport/dialog geometry, resolved alignment and query_one support, preserving every required-element and stale-evidence assertion plus the real mounted centering regressions?\nComplete fixture (Recommended): Repair the six demonstrated fixture failures without bypassing alignment checks or changing production behavior.\n\n2. The inspected stage PNGs and diagnostics locate the command-caret visibility failure between intact SVG underline styling and raster output; neither tested font declaration resolves it. Should the renewed plan use an export-only explicit thin underline derived from actual underlined terminal spans, preserving text, colors, coordinates, clips and terminal behavior, with a real raster visibility regression and fresh full-scene review?\nFaithful export underlines (Recommended): Represent the existing underline as SVG geometry; retain original evidence, supersampling and all twelve stage comparisons, without introducing bars or blocks over text."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"sql explorer: 1) if ctrl+shift+arrow up/down is pressed, then we should not spawn multiple cursors, instead selection should be expanded to the left until the line start, and next line until cursor's column (vs code like), it can be repeated multiple times to select many lines 2) now it seems that when multiple cursors is spawned, then I ctrl+c something and ctrl+v each cursor inserts WHOLE clipboard. instead each should have its own clipboard (VS code like)","task_id":"e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","version":2}